content.text:
This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:

   All work is in the **landing repo** (`~/Code/lobu-ai/landing`, private, Astro 6 + Preact 10), which is a different repo from the product repo (`~/Code/lobu`). Requests in this segment, in order:

   a. **"the theme of the app screenshot needs to match with what we have in the app"** — the homepage mock app plate (`HeroWindows.tsx`) was wearing the landing page's brutalist design language (red washes, mono-caps, square corners) instead of the real Lobu app's theme. Make it match the product.

   b. **"where is the url"** — asking for the local dev URL to preview.

   c. **"remove the right arrows here."** (with a screenshot of the sidebar showing `›` chevrons on the Memory and scout rows) — delete those disclosure chevrons.

   d. **"also you don't use these components in the blog post, maybe make these components dynamicly populated from config and put it into our blog post"** — the blog post was using static `.webp` screenshots while the mock components existed separately. Make the mock components config-driven and use them as the blog figures.

   Standing intent from earlier rounds (still governing): "mock must be exactly same as live screenshot ideally"; reuse the same components in the blog and on the homepage.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Landing stack: Astro 6, Preact 10, tailwind v4, hand-rolled `landing.css` with `--lp-*` tokens derived from `--color-page-*` / `--color-tg-*`
   - **CSS load path (corrected this session)**: `src/pages/blog/[...slug].astro` imports `src/globals.css`, whose line 2 is `@import "./components/landing/landing.css";` — so blog pages DO get all `.lp-hw-*` rules. (An earlier note in `ScreenshotFigure.tsx` claiming otherwise was wrong.)
   - Owletto app theme (`packages/owletto/src/index.css`) was ported 1:1 from the landing tokens: light bg `#FCFCFB`, dark bg `#0F0E0C`, card `#1A1815`, secondary/accent/sidebar-accent `#211E1A`, border `#2C2A25`, primary `#F5333A`, `--radius: 0.5rem`
   - shadcn conventions in the real app: rounded-full `Badge`, pill `Switch` with round thumb filled by `--primary`, sentence-case buttons with lucide icons
   - Real app routes (from `packages/owletto/src/app/`): `/$owner/connectors`, `/$owner/memory`, `/$owner/agents/$agentId/{chat,behaviors,skills,guardrails,permissions,conversations}`, `/$owner/agents/$agentId/chat/c/$id`
   - Public workspaces render anonymously (`market.lobu.ai/connectors`, `market.lobu.ai/memory`) — used as live ground truth
   - `agent-browser` CLI as the browser-automation fallback (Chrome extension was not connected)
   - Preact: fragments can't carry keys in a `.map()`; use `flatMap` returning keyed elements

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **`src/components/landing/landing.css`** (heavily modified)
     - New tokens in the `:root` block:
       ```css
       /* The app's `--accent`/`--sidebar-accent`: the neutral fill it uses for a
          selected row, an active segment, and an input well. */
       --lp-dim: var(--color-page-surface-dim);
       /* The app's `--radius`, halved. Only the app plate uses it; the rest of
          the page stays flat. */
       --lp-r: 6px;
       --lp-amber: #c8931f;
       ```
     - The single highest-leverage change — rebinding the wash inside the plate retints all 8 red-wash sites at once (`.lp-hw-grd .sw.on`, `.lp-hw-beh .bh:focus-visible`, `.lp-hw-beh .bh.on`, `.lp-hw-actbar .seg span.sel`, `.lp-hw-act .ev .fld .in`, `.lp-hw-act .ev.need`, `.lp-hw-aghd .mnu button:hover`, `.lp-hw-chat .tag`):
       ```css
       .lp-hw-win.app {
         /* This plate is a mock of our own product, so it wears the product's
            theme rather than the page's. In the app, selected rows, active
            segments and input wells are filled with the neutral `--accent`, and
            red is spent only on the primary action. Rebinding the wash here
            retints every pane at once. */
         --lp-wash: var(--lp-dim);
         left: 50%;
         width: min(640px, 54%);
         ...
       }
       ```
     - New static-flow variant so the same plate can sit in a blog figure:
       ```css
       /* The same plate placed in normal flow — a blog figure rather than a tile on
          the hero stage. Static, full width, and not draggable. */
       .lp-hw-win.app.st {
         position: static; left: auto; top: auto;
         width: 100%; margin-left: 0; cursor: default;
       }
       .lp-hw-win.app.st:hover { border-color: var(--lp-hair); }
       /* A figure has no neighbouring plates to stay level with, so it sizes to its
          own content instead of the stage's fixed height, and affords a wider
          sidebar than the hero can spare. */
       .lp-hw-win.app.st .lp-hw-split {
         height: auto; min-height: 240px;
         grid-template-columns: 168px minmax(0, 1fr);
       }
       ```
     - Sidebar rows now fill instead of colouring: `.lp-hw-side` gap `5px`→`1px`, padding `11px 10px`→`11px 8px`; `.ic`/`.ag`/`.cv` got `border-radius: var(--lp-r); padding: 4px 6px` + `background: var(--lp-dim)` on hover; `.lp-hw-side .sel { background: var(--lp-dim) }`; **deleted** `.sel .lp-hw-ni { color: var(--lp-red) }` and `.ag.sel .lp-hw-ni`
     - New `.lp-hw-side .org` block (workspace switcher) with `.wn`, `.cv-i`, `.sp`, `svg { width: 11px }`, and `.org .lp-hw-av { 15px, background: var(--lp-dim) }`
     - `.lp-hw-actbar .fc.on` neutralized: `color: var(--lp-ink2)`, `b { color: var(--lp-ink); font-weight: 600 }`, `::after { content: "×" }`
     - `.lp-hw-act .ev .btns .b` rewritten sentence-case sans with an `i` glyph slot; `.b.go` keeps the red fill
     - `.lp-hw-bolt` and `.lp-hw-act .ev .bolt` → `var(--lp-amber)`
     - Guardrail switch made a real pill: `.sw { border-radius: 999px }`, `.sw::after { border-radius: 50% }`, `.sw.on { background: var(--lp-red) }`, `.sw.on::after { background: var(--lp-on-red) }`
     - Connectors: `.cap` and `.st` → filled neutral pills (`border-radius: 999px; background: var(--lp-dim)`); `.lp-hw-conn` → `margin: 10px 13px; border: 1px solid var(--lp-hair); border-radius: var(--lp-r); overflow: hidden`
     - Memory: removed the `radial-gradient` dot grid from `.lp-hw-graph`; `.zm` is now borderless with no divider
     - Sentence-cased `.lp-hw-toolbar .mono`, `.pill`, `.lp-hw-foot .mono`, `.lp-hw-beh .lbl`/`.tg`, `.lp-hw-chain .ch`, `.lp-hw-composer .send`, `.lp-hw-ro .go`
     - **Deleted** the `.lp-hw-side .ic .chv, .lp-hw-side .ag .chv` rule
     - `.lp-hw-win.app .lp-hw-av { border-radius: var(--lp-r) }`

   - **`src/components/app-plate/AppPlate.tsx`** (NEW, 226 lines, untracked) — the shared, config-driven plate. Owns `NavIcon`, `AgentGlyph`, `CodeGlyph`, the org switcher, and the sidebar.
     ```tsx
     export type NavKey = "activity" | "connect" | "memory";
     export type SideRow =
       | { kind: "nav"; id: string; k: NavKey; label: string }
       | { kind: "group"; id: string; label: string }
       | { kind: "agent"; id: string; label: string }
       | { kind: "conv"; id: string; mark?: string; label: string };

     function RowBody({ row }: { row: Exclude<SideRow, { kind: "group" }> }) { ... }
     const ROW_CLASS = { nav: "ic", agent: "ag", conv: "cv" } as const;

     export function AppPlate({ org, path, rows, selected, onSelect, children }: {
       org: string;            // switcher name; first letter becomes the avatar
       path: string;           // route after app.lobu.ai
       rows: SideRow[];
       selected: string;       // id of the current row
       onSelect?: (id: string) => void;  // omit for an inert plate
       children: ComponentChildren;
     }) {
       // Remounting on pane change resets any open disclosure inside it.
       const paneKey = onSelect ? selected : undefined;
       ...
     }
     ```
     Rows render as `<button role="tab">` when `onSelect` is passed, `<span>` otherwise; `.lp-hw-main` gets `role="tabpanel"` only in the interactive case.

   - **`src/components/app-plate/ActivityPane.tsx`** (NEW, 159 lines, untracked) — config-driven Activity page.
     ```tsx
     export type ActivityField = { label: string; value: string; required?: boolean; placeholder?: boolean };
     export type ActivityEvent = {
       id: string; t: string; title: string;
       bolt?: boolean; mark?: string; on?: string; tag?: string; by?: string;
       kv?: { k: string; v: string }[];
       fields?: ActivityField[];
       actions?: boolean;
     };
     export type ActivityConfig = {
       tabs: string[];                                       // first entry is selected
       filters: { label: string; value: string; on?: boolean }[];
       count: string;
       events: ActivityEvent[];
       foot?: { left: string; right: string };
     };
     export function ActivityPane({ cfg }: { cfg: ActivityConfig }) { ... }
     ```
     The kv grid alternates cells, so pairs are flattened rather than wrapped:
     ```tsx
     {e.kv ? (
       <span class="kv">
         {e.kv.flatMap((r) => [
           <span class="k" key={`k${r.k}`}>{r.k}</span>,
           <span class="v" key={`v${r.k}`}>{r.v}</span>,
         ])}
       </span>
     ) : null}
     ```

   - **`src/components/blog/AppFigure.tsx`** (NEW, 64 lines, untracked) — the caption plate (border, mono `+` corner ticks, `FIG_nn` / label / right-aligned extra) wrapping live children instead of an `<img>`. Props `{ n, label, extra?, alt, children }`. Wraps children in `<div aria-label={alt} class="lp-hw-win app st" role="img">`.

   - **`src/components/landing/HeroWindows.tsx`** (heavily modified; 285 added / 378 deleted)
     - New imports and two config consts at the top:
       ```tsx
       import { type ActivityConfig, ActivityPane } from "../app-plate/ActivityPane";
       import { AgentGlyph, AppPlate, CodeGlyph, type SideRow } from "../app-plate/AppPlate";

       /**
        * The hero's sidebar. `id` doubles as the view the row selects, so the plate
        * needs no separate mapping from row to pane.
        */
       const SIDE_ROWS: SideRow[] = [
         { kind: "nav", id: "activity", k: "activity", label: "Activity" },
         { kind: "nav", id: "connect", k: "connect", label: "Connectors" },
         { kind: "nav", id: "memory", k: "memory", label: "Memory" },
         { kind: "group", id: "g-agents", label: "Agents" },
         { kind: "agent", id: "agent", label: "scout" },
         { kind: "group", id: "g-recent", label: "Recent" },
         { kind: "conv", id: "api", label: "Weekly risk report" },
         { kind: "conv", id: "slack", mark: "slack", label: "#acme renewal" },
         { kind: "conv", id: "chat", mark: "chatgpt", label: "At-risk accounts" },
         { kind: "conv", id: "claude", mark: "claude", label: "Q3 pipeline" },
       ];

       /** Both halves of the log in three rows: a proposal, an audit, an ingest. */
       const HERO_ACTIVITY: ActivityConfig = { tabs: [...], filters: [...], count: "4,545 items",
         foot: { left: "append-only", right: "1 awaiting approval" }, events: [ ...issue/audit/ingest... ] };
       ```
     - The centre plate now delegates:
       ```tsx
       <Win cls="app">
         <AppPlate onSelect={(id) => pick(id as typeof view)} org="Acme" path={path} rows={SIDE_ROWS} selected={view}>
           {view === "memory" ? <MemoryPane /> : null}
           {view === "activity" ? <ActivityPane cfg={HERO_ACTIVITY} /> : null}
           ...
         </AppPlate>
         <a class="lp-hw-act-link" href={getLobuBaseUrl()}>Open Lobu and start building →</a>
       </Win>
       ```
     - Address bar now covers transcripts:
       ```tsx
       : view === "slack" || view === "claude" || view === "api"
         ? // Every transcript, whatever surface it came in
           // on, is a conversation on the agent that owns it.
           `/acme/agents/scout/chat/c/${view === "slack" ? "s2f91c" : view === "claude" ? "c7a04e" : "a91bd3"}`
         : "/acme/activity";
       ```
       and Configure now points at `/acme/agents/scout/guardrails` (was `/skills`, which contradicted the selected tab).
     - Deleted local `CodeGlyph`, `AgentGlyph`, `NavIcon`, `BoltGlyph`, `ActivityPane`, both `class="chv"` spans, and the dead `.mk ai` / `.mk cl` modifier classes.

   - **`src/content/blog/self-improving-agents-are-event-sourced.mdx`** (modified) — figures are now live components:
     ```mdx
     import { AppFigure } from "../../components/blog/AppFigure";
     import { AppPlate } from "../../components/app-plate/AppPlate";
     import { ActivityPane } from "../../components/app-plate/ActivityPane";

     export const SIDE = [
       { kind: "nav", id: "activity", k: "activity", label: "Activity" },
       { kind: "nav", id: "connect", k: "connect", label: "Connectors" },
       { kind: "nav", id: "memory", k: "memory", label: "Memory" },
       { kind: "group", id: "g", label: "Agents" },
       { kind: "agent", id: "builder", label: "Builder" },
       { kind: "agent", id: "food", label: "food-ordering" },
     ];
     ```
     FIG_01 = `AppFigure` → `AppPlate org="Lobu Team" path="/lobu-team/activity"` → `ActivityPane` with a single pending "Create Issue" event (Title required / Labels placeholder / Repo name `lobu` / Repo owner `lobu-ai`, `actions: true`, `by: "Requested by REDACTED"`).
     FIG_02 = same plate with three events: `search_sdk completed` (5 kv rows incl. `Mcp session id`), `Inference provider 'gemini' created` (4 kv rows), and a `Rejected`-tagged `Create Issue`.

   - **Deleted**: `src/components/blog/ScreenshotFigure.tsx`, `public/blog/activity-approval.webp`, `public/blog/activity-audit.webp` (all verified unreferenced by grep first). `public/blog/entity-projection.webp` was already `git rm`'d in a prior round.

4. Errors and fixes:
   - **User rejected the plate's theme** ("the theme of the app screenshot needs to match with what we have in the app"). Fixed by sampling the real app's tokens and prod screenshots rather than guessing, then rebinding `--lp-wash` inside `.lp-hw-win.app` plus targeted radius/case/colour changes.
   - **`agent-browser` session died silently** — `screenshot` exited 0 but wrote no file. Fixed with `agent-browser close` then re-`open`.
   - **`agent-browser eval` shares scope across calls** — redeclaring `const r`/`q` threw "already been declared". Used unique identifiers each call (`w1`, `q1`, `sd2`, `fg2`, `q2`).
   - **`sips -Z` exited 13** on the webp — switched to Python PIL `im.thumbnail()` for all downscaling.
   - **Edit tool wouldn't match a 4-line Confirm/Reject block** despite identical text — narrowed the anchor to the two `<span class="b">` lines.
   - **tsc: `Property 'mark' does not exist on type '{ kind: "group" ... }'`** → `RowBody` param changed to `Exclude<SideRow, { kind: "group" }>`.
   - **tsc: `Cannot find name 'CodeGlyph'`** (still used by ChatPane rows) → added to the `../app-plate/AppPlate` import.
   - **Preact keys on a bare fragment** in the kv map → rewrote as `flatMap` returning two keyed spans.
